	Nethack 3.1 bugs (Amiga):

	The HackWB trashes options/etc settings it you try to change them from
there.  Use WB's Information window instead.

	Nethack corrupts the free memory list on occasion.  Probably write out
of bounds or write to freed mem. (I'll try it under mungwall and see if I can
catch it).

	Occasional crashes while quiting or saving (while it's writing the
icon for the save file).

	We have a network here; we'd like to have shared bones/high-scores.
This appears to be hard to do because of the way the levels are stored and
the way assigns are used.  It should be easy, Unix nethack does this.

